@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Managing NuGet, npm, Maven Packages";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="text-center lead">Managing packages effectively ensures secure and efficient dependency management for software development. Azure Artifacts allows teams to store, share, and manage packages using NuGet, npm, and Maven.</p>
    <hr />

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2>Why Manage Packages?</h2>
        <p>Software projects rely on external libraries and dependencies. Proper package management helps in:</p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Version Control:</strong> Ensuring applications use the correct library versions.</li>
            <li><strong>Security:</strong> Protecting against vulnerabilities in outdated dependencies.</li>
            <li><strong>Consistency:</strong> Avoiding dependency conflicts across development environments.</li>
            <li><strong>Efficiency:</strong> Reducing build times by caching frequently used packages.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="text-center mt-4">
        <img src="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/devops/artifacts/media/artifacts-overview.png" alt="Package Management in Azure DevOps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg">
        <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure Artifacts package feeds</small></p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Managing NuGet Packages</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Open Azure DevOps and navigate to <strong>Artifacts</strong>.</li>
            <li>Create a new feed and select <strong>NuGet</strong> as the package type.</li>
            <li>Use the following command to add the package source:
                <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">nuget sources Add -Name "AzureArtifacts" -Source "https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/{organization}/_packaging/{feed}/nuget/v3/index.json"</pre>
            </li>
            <li>Push packages using:
                <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">nuget push package.nupkg -Source "AzureArtifacts" -ApiKey az</pre>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Managing npm Packages</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Create an npm feed in Azure Artifacts.</li>
            <li>Authenticate with:
                <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">npm login --registry=https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/{organization}/_packaging/{feed}/npm/registry/</pre>
            </li>
            <li>Publish a package:
                <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">npm publish --registry=https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/{organization}/_packaging/{feed}/npm/registry/</pre>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Managing Maven Packages</h3>
        <ol>
            <li>Create a Maven feed in Azure Artifacts.</li>
            <li>Add the repository to the Maven settings.xml:
                <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">&lt;repository&gt;
    &lt;id&gt;azure-artifacts&lt;/id&gt;
    &lt;url&gt;https://pkgs.dev.azure.com/{organization}/_packaging/{feed}/maven/v1&lt;/url&gt;
&lt;/repository&gt;</pre>
            </li>
            <li>Deploy a package using:
                <pre class="bg-light p-3 rounded">mvn deploy</pre>
            </li>
        </ol>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <h3>Best Practices for Package Management</h3>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Use separate feeds</strong> for development, testing, and production.</li>
            <li><strong>Automate package updates</strong> through CI/CD pipelines.</li>
            <li><strong>Apply retention policies</strong> to clean up old versions.</li>
            <li><strong>Enable security scanning</strong> to detect vulnerabilities in dependencies.</li>
        </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-5">
        <p>Effective package management with Azure Artifacts ensures stability, security, and scalability for software projects. By integrating package management with CI/CD pipelines, teams can streamline development workflows.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="d-flex justify-content-between mt-4">
        <a href="@Url.Action("IntroAzureArtifacts", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">&larr; Previous: Introduction to Azure Artifacts</a>
        <a href="@Url.Action("IntegrateArtifactsCICD", "AzureDevOps")" class="btn btn-outline-secondary">Next: Integrating Artifacts CI/CD &rarr;</a>
    </div>
</div>